# muse Tier-0: identity/alias/wake-guidance foundations (poll fallback)

## Goal

`muse` works as a c2c peer with ZERO muse cooperation: CLI-only
poll/peek/send/whoami/list/rooms from any muse shell, correct alias
minting, honest NONE wake row + Monitor recipe. No hooks, no MCP, no
managed start. Can start before B352 lands (identity-key arms take
provisional values, finalized after the P3 verdict).

## Contract (exact touch points; line refs verified 2026-10-02)

- Alias: free `muse-…` via `C2c_start.default_alias_prefix`
  (`ocaml/c2c_start.ml:3644`, identity default) — no code.
- Blocklist: add `muse` + `muse-` in `ocaml/c2c_blocklist.ml:5–72`
  (B182 keep-in-sync; keep `test_c2c_cli.ml:583` prefix-list green).
- Inference (`ocaml/c2c_mcp_helpers_post_broker.ml`): native key row in
  `native_session_id_env_keys` :710–721 (provisional: `MUSE_SESSION_ID`
  if P3 confirms, else `[]` like cursor + documented fallback);
  `inferred_client_type_from_env` :875–892 precedence arm (place AFTER
  established natives; document why); flows into init/send/whoami/MCP.
- Send sniff: `infer_send_auto_register_client` arm in
  `ocaml/cli/c2c_send_cmd.ml:23–87` (note: agy/hermes have no arm —
  muse MUST have one so sends from muse shells self-register).
- Wake guidance: `advice "muse"` arms (Install + Managed_start) in
  `ocaml/c2c_wake_guidance.ml:29–173` (NONE + Monitor recipe, verbatim
  #414); footer flows via `do_install_client` automatically.
- Detect: `path_detectable_clients` row (`ocaml/cli/c2c_init_cmd.ml:41–49`,
  `muse` binary) + `detect_client_prefixes`
  (`ocaml/cli/c2c_setup.ml:2046`, managed-sid prefix match).
- Health/dashboard: `"muse"` in `supported_clients`
  (`ocaml/cli/c2c_health_cmd.ml:564`).
- Detect-agent markers: muse env keys in
  `ocaml/cli/c2c_detect_agent_cmd.ml:23–39`.
- Landing copy: CLI-first arm in `ocaml/cli/c2c_root_cmd.ml:137–164`
  (must NOT fall into the "c2c MCP ready" default).
- Skill (only if a muse skills dir fits without a spike): embedded
  `C2c_muse_skill_embedded` + `write/refresh_muse_skill_if_stale`
  following `c2c_setup.ml:44–135`; body MUST be identity-agnostic
  (#83: never bake alias/sid/queued-count into a shared file).

## Acceptance

- From a muse shell with `C2C_MCP_SESSION_ID` (or native key post-P3):
  `c2c whoami`, `send`, `poll-inbox`, `peek-inbox`, `wait-inbox`,
  `list`, `rooms` all work; alias mints as `muse-…`; sticky alias +
  B135/B188/B191 behavior matches other clients.
- `c2c health` shows muse row; landing page names muse correctly.
- Provisional identity arms replaced/confirmed after B352 P3.
- Tests: inference unit tests (env→sid/client-type matrix),
  send-sniff test, wake-guidance pure tests
  (`test_c2c_wake_guidance.ml` arms), blocklist tests.
- Live proof: muse↔claude (or codex) poll round-trip recorded.

Acceptance hygiene (parent review): provisional-arms line resolves to confirmed-kept per B352 P3 U2; stale PROVISIONAL comments refreshed post-merge. M3 (wake-arm surfacing) + M5 (init --with-mcp message) remain as future follow-ups.